freeze-trust-policy-at-server-start

Lane: mixed

Unit: configure-trust-bypasses-at-server-start

ChildPatch: freeze-trust-policy-at-server-start

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema-snapshot

Purpose: Choose independent project and hook trust bypasses only at App Server startup, including daemon launches, and preserve that immutable policy throughout each server lifetime.

Requires: none

Provides: Publish startup policy through initialize, persist managed launch choices under the existing daemon operation lock, reject conflicting client assertions without restarting or replacing the server, admit project sources and enabled hooks under independent startup bypasses, and make TUI consent and all configuration reloads consume the same policy.

Boundary: Persisted project and hook trust entries, explicit hook enablement, sandbox and managed restrictions, existing daemon feature recovery and remote-control enrollment remain independently owned; no live daemon restart or user configuration edit is part of this change.

Verification: Focused configuration and hook tests cover effective admission, unchanged trust and permissions, plugin runtime review bypass and reload stability; protocol, daemon and TUI tests cover omitted and matching assertions, conflicts on start/resume/fork, no shared-server mutation or fallback, and CLI true/false parsing.


